From 0a1f499f67ce452e500100f4222f6210fb932c55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:28:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zones: Tiling follows the usable area and the outputs

The tiling cells were computed when a window came or went, never when the
usable area changed: a Dock, Clip or panel with an exclusive zone that
appeared, moved or went away left the cells under it (or a gap) until the
user asked to apply again; same after an output was plugged, unplugged or
changed mode or scale.

The toolkit raises wlmtk_desktop_events_t::usable_area_changed when the
usable area of an output changes (only then: a panel without exclusive
zone does not), and zones relayouts on it and on the output layout's
change signal (closing the picker and the overlay).

Tests: unit test layer usable_area_signal; wmake-zones' Wayland
functional suite with a layer-shell panel with an exclusive zone (47/47;
without this change the panel case fails). ctest 29/29.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
